Rule 6 (index tensor (v_3) is within the input tensor (v_1) along the specified dimension (v_2))
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ shape(v_1, v_2) - 1
>>
Rule 7 (If dim is negative, the absolute value cannot exceed ndim(input))
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 < 0 then 0 - v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 8 (When reduce is "constant", src must be a NUMBER)
{v_1 : str} |= if v_1 = "constant" then true
>>
Rule 9 (If dim is specified, index values should be valid.)
{v_1: int, v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_2,0)-1] : v_3[i] < shape(v_2, v_1)
